{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Of the children of Zebulun, etc.</b> The verse alludes to their deeds and to what may be grasped from it: סרד — like סֵדֶר (order). And so is the way of Scripture to call a keves (lamb) a kesev; and the intention in this is that he [Zebulun] would arrange before Issachar everything he needed for his sustenance. And 'Elon' is an expression of strength (חוזק), alluding, as it were, to what Scripture says (Proverbs 3:18) ״עֵץ חַיִּים הִיא לַמַּחֲזִיקִים בָּהּ״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Leviticus Rabbah 25:1) that it was not said 'to those who learn it' but rather 'to those who hold fast to it,' etc. Therefore, since Zebulun would sustain (מחזיק) those who learn Torah, He ascribed to him this quality — and this is the meaning of saying 'Elon.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The word סרד is given as a metathesis or inverted form of סדר (order); both the term itself and the keves/kesev example illustrate the phenomenon of letter reversal (Atbash-style or simple transposition) that the Or HaChaim detects as an allusion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:51.890291981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}